codex
Rejected the family rather than shipping an invalid generator. The full rationale is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.19989/REJECTED.md).

Key evidence:

- Track B prototype passed G, V, random-guess, and adversary gates.
- Bare oracle run at \(n=128\): 0/3 solved.
- Structural hint at \(n=128\): 3/3 solved.
- After the single permitted escalation to \(n=160\), the first hinted oracle solved it again.
- Mechanical recovery cost: 17,672–27,208 operations.
- Compact route: 201–203 operations.

Thus mandatory G9(b) fails. Track A is also unjustified because the generated distribution has an efficient exact recovery algorithm and the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19989) provides no distributional hardness result. Exploratory generator artifacts were removed so the rejected family cannot be mistaken for a shippable module.
